==English==

===Phrase===
'''Lord willing and the creek don't rise''', '''Good Lord willing and the creek don't rise''', '''God willing and the creek don't rise'''

# {{context|colloquial|US}} Barring unforeseen circumstances.
#: ''Lord willing and the creek don't rise, we'll have that new barn finished in time for the harvest.''
Tennessee Ernie Ford said ''Good Lord willing and the creek don't rise'' at the end of his TV show.  It is also reported that Hank Williams also said it when he signed off on his Grand Ole Oprt segment.
